{"id":80,"text":"Daniel and his friends were playing football in the street when his shot went wrong. The ball flew through the window of Mrs. Kelly’s house, and the glass smashed loudly.\n\nHis friends ran away at once. Daniel hesitated. He could hear his own heart beating. He could run home and pretend that nothing had happened. Nobody had seen him.\n\nBut he looked at the broken glass and imagined the old woman sitting alone in the cold. He knew she couldn’t afford to fix the window easily. He took a deep breath, walked up to the door and knocked.\n\n“Mrs. Kelly,” he said, with a shaking voice, “I broke your window. I’m very sorry. I’d like to pay for it, but I don’t have much money. Can I work for you instead?”\n\nThe old woman looked at him for a long moment. “Most boys would have run away,” she said. “Come in.”\n\nFor the next month, Daniel mowed her lawn, did her shopping and cleaned her garden every weekend. In the end, they became friends. She baked him cakes and told him stories about her youth.\n\nYears later, Daniel often said that it was the best mistake he ever made. “Running away would have been easy,” he said. “But I would never have met the person who taught me what responsibility means.”\n\nMoral: Admitting your mistakes takes courage, and it can turn a bad moment into a good one.","tr":null,"gl":{"daniel":"Doniyor (ism)","and":"va","his":"uning","friends":"do'stlar","were":"edi(lar)","playing":"o'ynab; chalib","football":"futbol","in":"ichida, -da","the":"(aniq artikl)","street":"ko'cha","when":"qachon; -ganda","shot":"otilib chiqdi (tez o'sdi)","went":"bordi, ketdi","wrong":"noto'g'ri","ball":"to'p","flew":"uchdi","through":"orqali","window":"deraza","of":"-ning; -dan","mrs":"xonim","kelly":"Kelli (ism)","house":"uy","glass":"shisha","smashed":"chil-chil qildi","loudly":"baland ovozda","ran":"yugurdi","away":"uzoqqa, nari","at":"-da, -ga","once":"bir marta; bir paytlar","hesitated":"ikkilandi","he":"u (erkak)","could":"qila olardi","hear":"eshitm